  "question": {
    "text": "A soap bubble is blown to a diameter of $7 \\mathrm{~cm} .36960 \\mathrm{erg}$ of work is done in blowing it further. If surface tension of soap solution is $40 \\mathrm{dyne} / \\mathrm{cm}$ then the new radius is______ $\\mathrm{cm}$ Take $\\left(\\pi=\\frac{22}{7}\\right)$",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "7",
  "solution": {
    "text": "$\\begin{aligned} & \\omega=\\Delta \\mathrm{U}=\\mathrm{S} \\Delta \\mathrm{A} \\\\ & 36960 \\mathrm{erg}=\\frac{40 \\text { dyne }}{\\mathrm{cm}} 8 \\pi\\left[(\\mathrm{r})^2-\\left(\\frac{7}{2}\\right)^2\\right] \\mathrm{cm}^2 \\\\ & \\mathrm{r}=7 \\mathrm{~cm}\\end{aligned}$",
    "image": null
  },
